    {"text": "Tested obs-rust 0.1.0-beta.20261018 (Linux AppImage, Fedora/Bazzite, kernel 7.2.9) with a fresh config and a copy of my scene collection with the truncated values put back: Elgato 4K X \"framerate\": 60 (NV12 2560x1440) and Logitech BRIO \"framerate\": 30 (MJPG 3840x2160). - The log shows Framerate: 60.00 fps for the 4K X, and v4l2-ctl --get-parm reports 60/1 (stock OBS ran it at 144). The BRIO shows 30.00 / 30/1. - Toggling Use Buffering on the 4K X did not restart the capture. - After saving, the collection holds \"framerate\": 4294967356 for the 4K X and 4294967326 for the BRIO. All three behaviors confirmed. Thanks for the fix!", "login": "jrsallee", "url": "https://github.com/obs-rust/obs-studio/issues/1117#issuecomment-6250423489", "date": "2026-10-18", "status": "approved", "issue": 1117},
